# Quiet mode, on the configsettings page of the instr selector.
# A .ui entry is not run as a program: Nebulae itself handles it (ui.py,
# mode = the name after the number, here "quiet").
# Speed click on it: the speed encoder picks the level, shown in the colour
# of both speed LEDs: off = red, Quiet 1 = green, Quiet 2 = blue,
# Quiet 3 = yellow.
# Speed click switches to it (saved by configsettings.py, switched by
# Code/scripts/quiet.sh) and goes back to
# the instrument; pitch click goes back without a change.
#   Quiet 1: everything not needed to play off, also LAN and the Wi-Fi chip
#   Quiet 2: as 1, but LAN on and Wi-Fi possible
#   Quiet 3: as 2, but the file and freeze LEDs dim (PWM) like the others
# Slot LED bright = a level is on (nebulae-status).
